    "definitions": {
      "short": "the breast of a woman or animal (as bulging)",
      "usage": "breast, pap, teat.",
      "full": "H7699. shad [ שַׁד ] noun masculine Hosea 9:14 female breast ; — absolute שָׁ֑ד Lam 4:3 ; elsewhere dual שָׁדַיִם Hosea 9:14 +, construct שְׁדֵי Ezek 23:21 +, suffix שָׁדַי Song 1:13 ; 8:10 , שָׁדַיִךְ 4:5 +, etc.; — breast: 1 of woman Hosea 2:4 ; Ezek 16:7 ; 23:3 , 21 ( נְעוּרָ֑יִךְ שְׁדֵי , || דַּדַּיִךְ ), 23:34 (&gt; strike out ᵐ5 Manuscripts Co; — all these of personified People), Song 1:13 ; 4:5 ; 7:4 , 8 , 9 ; 8:8 , 10 ; of mother Psa 22:10 , with יָנַק suck Song 8:1 ; Job 3:12 ; Joel 2:15 ; Hosea 9:14 (see [ צָמַק ]); עֲתִיקֵי ׳מִשּׁ Isa 28:9 i.e. those already weaned, mature (|| מֵךְָלָב גְּמוּלֵי ). — 32:12 see [ ספד ]. 2 of animal Lam 4:3 . 3 both human and animal , שׁ ׳בִּרְכוֺת וָרָ֑חַם Gen 49:25 (poem in J). II. שֹׁד noun masculine id. (compare the rare Arabic , Lane 333 Ba ZMG ii. 637 ); — ׳שׁ absolute, of mother Job 24:9 ; construct (figurative, with יָנַק ): ׳שׁ מְלָכִים Isa 60:16 , ׳שׁ תַּנְחֻמֶיהָ 66:11 , i.e. the consolations of Jerusalem.",
      "rootNote": "or שֹׁד ; probably from 7736 (in its original sense) contracted;",
      "sources": [
        "MorphHB occurrences",
        "Strong Hebrew Dictionary",
        "Brown-Driver-Briggs"
      ]
    },
